package org.verapdf.model.baselayer;

% READING GUIDE: .mdl files describe validation contracts, not executable Java.
% Xtext generates Java interfaces; parser-backed implementations supply the values.
% A property exposes a scalar fact; a link exposes another model object for traversal.
% Link suffixes describe multiplicity: ? optional, * zero or more, + one or more.
% An unsuffixed link describes one target; check generated APIs for its representation.
% Validation must still represent malformed PDFs, so multiplicity is not a reason
% to invent missing objects or discard invalid input before rules can inspect it.
%
% C# PORT: Use a shared model interface (for example IModelObject), not System.Object.
% Model "extends" becomes interface inheritance when porting the generated contracts.
% Keep parser objects separate from these validation views and preserve model type names.
% See README.md for scalar mappings, link collections and generator considerations.
% Root object for the complete hierarchy of PDF types
type Object {

}
